  "VEI is the Volcanic Explosivity Index — the erupted volume and plume height of one eruption on a 0–8 scale, as recorded by the Global Volcanism Program. It is the only structured measure of eruptive size the catalog carries; an eruption STYLE (Strombolian, Vulcanian, Plinian…) is not a field in that database and is therefore not shown here as if it were.": "VEI 是火山爆發指數 —— 由 GVP 記錄的單次噴發噴出量與噴煙高度，以 0〜8 表示。這是目錄中唯一結構化的噴發規模量度；「噴發型式」（斯通博利式、伏爾坎寧式、普林尼式等）不是該資料庫的欄位，因此此處不會將其當作既有資料呈現。",
